      "predicate": "iadas:authorConclusion",
      "object": "The findings confirm the strong relationship between body dissatisfaction and dieting as found in previous studies. Concern over mistakes was also found to impact upon performance cognitive anxiety, which confirms previous work. The study also shows that prevention of eating disorders among dancers may required less of a focus on dieting, and more in reducing specific parts of the individuals personality, concerns over mistakes."
    },
    {
      "predicate": "iadas:limites",
      "object": "The main limitation is the use of general questionnaires such as the BDI II or EAT-26 which are not validated specifically to be used within the dance population, although they are validated and highly reliable measurements. Another limitation is that performance anxiety was measured hypothetically and it will be best to measure it previous to an event, which due to the methodology of our current study this was not possible."
    },
